---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Our Network" description="A community radio network, built by volunteers and powered by the sun, that helps Western New Yorkers stay in touch when other systems are down.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Our network"
    title="A network built by neighbors"
    intro="Small radios, solar power, and a lot of help from the community. Here's what it is and how you can be part of it."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        Our community network is a web of small, low-power radios spread across Western New York.
        Each one can pass a short text message along to the next, so a message can travel across
        town and beyond without cell towers, internet, or the power grid.
      </p>
      <p>
        Repeaters on rooftops and other high places help messages travel farther. Many run on
        solar panels and batteries, so they keep working through an outage.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it's for</h2>
      <p>
        Everyone. Families checking on each other after a storm, neighbors looking out for one
        another, and community groups that want a dependable backup. You don't need a license or
        a technical background to use it.
      </p>

      <div class="notice">
        <p>The network is a community backup for staying in touch. It is not monitored by emergency services. <strong>Always call 911 in an emergency if you can.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-badge"><Icon name="radio" /></div>
          <h3>Join the network</h3>
          <p>
            Our network currently runs on a system called MeshCore. Everything you need to get
            started, including which radio to get, setup guides, the coverage map, and our friendly
            Discord community, is on our network site.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href={site.networkSite.url}>Visit {site.networkSite.name}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="icon-badge"><Icon name="home" /></div>
          <h3>Host a repeater</h3>
          <p>
            A tall building, a sunny rooftop, or a spot with a wide view can help a whole
            neighborhood stay connected. If you can offer a location, we'd love to talk.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn--soft" href="/get-involved/">Offer a location</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
